# 11. GROUP BY with HAVING

**Q:** Find departments with an average salary greater than 60000.

### Query

```sql
SELECT department,
       AVG(salary) AS average_salary
FROM employees
GROUP BY department
HAVING AVG(salary) > 60000;
```

### Learning Point

You cannot normally use an aggregate condition such as:

```sql
WHERE AVG(salary) > 60000
```

because `WHERE` works before grouping.

Use:

```sql
HAVING AVG(salary) > 60000
```

because `HAVING` filters grouped results.

