# 17. INSERT INTO ... SELECT

**Q:** Insert into `high_salary_employees` all employees earning more than 70000.

### Query

```sql
INSERT INTO high_salary_employees
(employee_id, name, salary, department)
SELECT employee_id,
       name,
       salary,
       department
FROM employees
WHERE salary > 70000;
```

### Learning Point

There are two major INSERT styles:

### 1. INSERT ... VALUES

Manually specified data:

```sql
INSERT INTO users
(user_id, username, status)
VALUES
(1, 'testuser', 'ACTIVE');
```

### 2. INSERT ... SELECT

Copy rows from another table/query:

```sql
INSERT INTO high_salary_employees
(employee_id, name, salary, department)
SELECT employee_id,
       name,
       salary,
       department
FROM employees
WHERE salary > 70000;
```

The `SELECT` can return:

```text
0 rows
1 row
100 rows
10,000 rows
```

and all matching rows can be inserted.

### QA Testing Usage

This is commonly useful for creating test data:

```sql
INSERT INTO users
(user_id, username, status)
VALUES
(1, 'testuser', 'ACTIVE');
```

For backup/copying:

```sql
INSERT INTO users_backup
SELECT *
FROM users;
```

