# 20. FULL OUTER JOIN

**Q:** Find all customers and their orders, including customers with no orders and orders with no customers.

### Query

```sql
SELECT c.customer_name,
       o.order_id,
       o.order_date
FROM customers c
FULL OUTER JOIN orders o
ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id;
```

### Learning Point

`FULL OUTER JOIN` keeps:

```text
Matching customers/orders
+
Customers without orders
+
Orders without customers
```

Conceptually:

```text
Customers        Orders
    \              /
     \            /
      FULL JOIN
```

